From 3e9eb1651e97a13f74a95caed693a7bf936cee82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: run Solid's capability linker in production client
 builds

Adds `solidCapabilities` from `@solidjs/compiler/capabilities` to `vite
build` by default: each client environment's module graph is proven from
its compiled output and the library manifests, and `@solidjs/signals` is
linked against the async-free entry and/or with unused feature switches
compiled out. Anything unproven keeps the full runtime.

- New option `capabilities?: boolean | CapabilitiesOptions` (default
  true; `false` opts out). The object form forwards `features`,
  `compiledFacts`, `compiledSeams`, `typedSummary`, `report`, `entries`
  to the linker; `server: true` also links server environments.
- One linker per environment via `applyToEnvironment` (builder mode,
  start, SSR); the environment's resolved config is handed to the
  linker's `configResolved`.
- Dev and vitest keep the full runtime; a hand-wired `solidCapabilities()`
  wins; a compiler without the linker builds unchanged (logged once).
- `pnpm test:unit`: node:test coverage of the wiring against a fixture
  linker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
