+---
+'@solidjs/vite-plugin': minor
+---
+
+Production client builds now run Solid's capability linker (`solidCapabilities` from `@solidjs/compiler/capabilities`) by default. The linker proves each client module graph from its compiled output and the library packages' capability manifests, then links `@solidjs/signals` against the smallest runtime the graph can use: the async-free entry when the graph is proven async-free, and every runtime feature switch (optimistic updates, verdicts, stores, snapshots, iterable blocks, compiled seams) the graph is proven not to use compiled out. Anything unproven keeps the full runtime. New option `capabilities?: boolean | CapabilitiesOptions` (default `true`): `false` opts out; an object tunes the linker (`features`, `compiledFacts`, `compiledSeams`, `typedSummary`, `report`, `entries`) and `server: true` also links server environments (off by default). The dev server and vitest keep the full runtime. A config that already adds `solidCapabilities()` keeps its own instance, and an `@solidjs/compiler` without the linker builds exactly as before.
